For clarity, the respective spike sparsity rates are defined as follows: R i ​ n ¯ \overline{R_{in}} denotes the input spike rate entering the transformer block; R K ​ V ¯ \overline{R_{KV}} represents the activation sparsity following the Key-Value (KV) matrix summation; R Q ​ K ​ V ¯ \overline{R_{QKV}} signifies the spike sparsity emerging from the core attention computation f ⁡ ( Q , K , V ) f(Q,K,V) ;
and R M ​ L ​ P n ¯ \overline{R_{MLP_{n}}} denotes the spike rate propagating from the respective linear layers within the MLP block.
Correspondingly, the DSN’s non-dormant activity factors D ¯ \overline{D} are applied to the postsynaptic neurons in each internal module, enabling multiplicative reductions in computational cost throughout the self-attention mechanism.

